# Three.js Axis Conversion (Y-up to Z-up)

## Purpose
Convert Three.js Y-up scenes to Blender Z-up orientation while preserving object positions in the target space.

## Setup
- Requires `three`.

## Usage
```js
import * as THREE from 'three';

function wrapZUp(object) {
  const wrapper = new THREE.Group();
  wrapper.rotation.x = -Math.PI / 2; // Y-up to Z-up
  wrapper.add(object);
  wrapper.updateMatrixWorld(true);
  return wrapper;
}
```

## Notes
- Apply the rotation at a top-level wrapper so local transforms remain intact.
- Call `updateMatrixWorld(true)` before export to bake the rotation into `matrixWorld`.
- The exporter should use world matrices to emit correctly oriented vertices.
